 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S445-025\",\n \"clauses\": {\"determine\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F24\", \"template\": \"What place is the digit {digit} in, in the number {number}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F24 asks the learner to determine the place of a digit in a number. Its number runs are all 4-digit (1095 to 9870), and its digit runs cover 0 to 9.\"},\n  \"place_value_of_digit\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F23\", \"template\": \"What is the {pv_label} of the digit {digit} in {number}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F23 asks for the place value of a digit. pv_label is nested from F01, which prints the gated word 'place value', which is in cumulative_vocab.\"},\n  \"4_digit_number\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F22\", \"template\": \"In {number}, what digit is in the {place_name} place?\", \"reasoning\": \"F22 presents a 4-digit number in every render (printed_runs from 1095 to 9105, all 4-digit). Its question is answerable in the grade 3 frame.\"},\n  \"value_of_digit\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F12\", \"template\": \"The {val_phrase} of {digit} in {number} is {value}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F12 expresses the value of a digit. val_phrase is nested from F02, which prints 'worth' because 'value' is not in cumulative_vocab. F12 is in hints only. F19 also addresses this clause but prints the ungated word 'value' (see failing_templates), so it is not the producing family.\"},\n  \"digit_of_number\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F22\", \"template\": \"In {number}, what digit is in the {place_name} place?\", \"reasoning\": \"F22 asks for the digit of a 4-digit number, identified by place.\"},\n  \"given_place_value\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F22\", \"template\": \"In {number}, what digit is in the {place_name} place?\", \"reasoning\": \"F22 gives the place (place_name from ones, tens, hundreds, thousands) and asks for the digit in it, which is the digit given its place value.\"}\n },\n \"failing_families\": [\"F19\", \"F20\", \"F21\"],\n \"failing_templates\": [\"In the number {number}, the value of the digit {digit} in the {place} place is {fill_value}\", \"{question_text} The answer is {fill_value}.\", \"{statement}. True or False?\"],\n \"overall\": \"FAIL\",\n \"reasoning\": \"F19 prints the word 'value' in its literal text. 'value' is not in cumulative_vocab, and F02's vocabulary gate (requires_vocab 'value', prints 'worth', words_left_out 1) says this lc must print 'worth' instead, so F19 breaks the gate. F19's fill_value has two domains. The keyed-true domain lists only 5, with no derived_from_values, so the digit, place and fill_value slots are independent: a statement can be keyed true while digit and place do not make 5 true. F20 nests question_text from F22 or F24, which are questions asking for a digit or a place, and appends fill_value. Its keyed-true fill_value domain includes place names ('hundreds', 'ones', 'tens' from the place list) and 0, 5, 6, and its distractor domain includes values such as 2000 and 202. So a what-digit question can be followed by a place name or 2000 as 'The answer is'. F21 appends '. True or False?' to a statement that F20 already ends with a period, so the text reads with a double period, and it applies true-or-false to a question sentence. F01, F02, F03 to F18 and F22 to F24 were checked and print only gate-permitted words, place names, or 4-digit numbers, with no fault found in their own templates.\"}",
